  "grammar": [
    {
      "title": "Numbers with nouns",
      "body": "The number comes **before** the noun. 'One' has a special attributive form **ഒരു** *oru* (ഒരു ചായ 'one tea'); the others are often said with a final -u before a noun: രണ്ടു, മൂന്നു, നാലു (written either രണ്ട് or രണ്ടു).\n\nAfter a number, people-nouns usually take the plural (മൂന്ന് കുട്ടികൾ 'three children'), but things often stay singular in everyday speech (രണ്ട് ചായ 'two teas').\n\nTo count people, use **പേർ** *pēr* ('persons'): രണ്ടു പേർ 'two people', എത്ര പേർ? 'how many people?'. Adding **-ഉം** to a number means 'all of them': രണ്ടും 'both', മൂന്നും 'all three'.",
      "examples": [
        { "native": "ഒരു വീട്", "roman": "oru vīṭŭ", "en": "a house / one house" },
        { "native": "മൂന്ന് കുട്ടികൾ", "roman": "mūnnŭ kuṭṭikaḷ", "en": "three children" },
        { "native": "രണ്ട് ചായ", "roman": "raṇḍŭ chāya", "en": "two teas" },
        { "native": "അഞ്ചു പേർ", "roman": "añju pēr", "en": "five people" },
        { "native": "രണ്ടുപേരും വന്നു.", "roman": "raṇḍupērum vannu.", "en": "Both (people) came." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "How many, how old, which one",
      "body": "**എത്ര** *etra* asks 'how many / how much'. It also asks for numbers in general (phone number, time, price).\n\n**Age** is expressed as years that have 'become' (ആയി *āyi*, 'became') to someone, with the dative: എനിക്ക് മുപ്പത് **വയസ്സായി** 'I'm thirty'. For children you'll also hear അവന് അഞ്ചു വയസ്സുണ്ട് 'he has five years'.\n\n**Ordinals**: add **-ആമത്തെ** (-āmatte) to the number: രണ്ടാമത്തെ 'second', പത്താമത്തെ 'tenth'. ആദ്യത്തെ *ādyatte* 'first' and അവസാനത്തെ *avasānatte* 'last' are very common. Shorter -ആം forms appear in fixed expressions: ഒന്നാം ക്ലാസ് 'first standard (grade 1)'.",
      "examples": [
        { "native": "എത്ര കുട്ടികൾ ഉണ്ട്?", "roman": "etra kuṭṭikaḷ uṇḍŭ?", "en": "How many children are there?" },
        { "native": "അവന് എത്ര വയസ്സായി?", "roman": "avanŭ etra vayassāyi?", "en": "How old is he?" },
        { "native": "അമ്മൂമ്മയ്ക്ക് എൺപത് വയസ്സായി.", "roman": "ammūmmaykkŭ eṇpatŭ vayassāyi.", "en": "Grandma is eighty." },
        { "native": "മൂന്നാമത്തെ വീട്", "roman": "mūnnāmatte vīṭŭ", "en": "the third house" },
        { "native": "അവൾ ഏഴാം ക്ലാസ്സിൽ പഠിക്കുന്നു.", "roman": "avaḷ ēḻām klāssil paṭhikkunnu.", "en": "She studies in seventh standard." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "dialogue": {
    "title": "Grandma meets a new neighbour's child",
    "setting": "Ammooma (grandmother) talks to Anu, a little girl, on the veranda.",
    "lines": [
      { "speaker": "Ammooma", "native": "മോളുടെ പേരെന്താ?", "roman": "mōḷuṭe pērendā?", "en": "What's your name, dear? (lit. daughter's name?)" },
