  "culture": "Indian number grouping is used in Kerala: 1,00,000 is one lakh and 1,00,00,000 is one crore, and prices, salaries and populations are always quoted this way. Children and younger people (even adults) are often affectionately called മോൻ / മോൾ (son / daughter) by older people — Ammooma's മോളുടെ പേരെന്താ? is completely natural even to a stranger's child.",
